  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given slope at (x, y) is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>dy</mtext><mtext>dx</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>y</mtext><mtext>x</mtext></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mtext>sec</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math><br />let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>y</mtext><mtext>x</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mtext>t</mtext><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>y</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>xt</mtext></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Differentiating this wrt&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mfrac><mtext>dy</mtext><mtext>dx</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mtext>t</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>x</mtext><mfrac><mtext>dt</mtext><mtext>dx</mtext></mfrac></math>......<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now using equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, we have<br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>t</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>x</mtext> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>dt</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>dx</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>t</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>sec</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>t</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Integrating both sides.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mtext>dt</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mtext>x</mtext></mfrac><mtext>dx</mtext></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mtext>c</mtext></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Now Put value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> in above equation.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>sin</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mtext>c</mtext></math>.....<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Given that curve passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>,&#160;</mtext><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;so put in above equation.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>sin</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mtext>c</mtext><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>c</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, put the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;in equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>sin</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
